  "title": "MOVING2024: Motor imagery / motor execution dataset from the MOVING study",
  "description": "A multi-modal dataset of 32-channel dry-electrode EEG recorded together with Virtual Glove hand-kinematic tracking during motor imagery and motor execution of three right-hand movements (open/close, wrist rotation, finger tapping). Eleven healthy participants completed a rest, motor imagery, motor execution sequence with eight repetitions of the triplet. This BIDS re-release was produced via MOABB from the published MOVING dataset.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was acquired with a Neuroelectrics Enobio 32 dry-electrode wireless system (32 channels, 500 Hz, 10-20 montage, CMS/DRL reference). Each trial involved a cue-based visual protocol with 2 s fixation and 6 s action, repeated eight times per movement triplet per subject (about 10 minutes), with rest, motor imagery and motor execution phases.",
